# Lines tools/qemu-test must see, in this order, as whole serial lines.
# In QEMU: the entropy PD passes its start-up
# tests and fills the consumer's seed ring before the consumer runs (it runs
# above it); the consumer is refused before its first seed, keys its generator
# from one and wipes its copies, prints the SHA-256 of a draw (the line after,
# not checked: it differs every run) and never the bytes; the entropy PD
# overwrites the slot it took, which the consumer checks.
NOWAYOS: entropy: starting
NOWAYOS: entropy: virtio-rng on transport 8, claimed to give 8 bits a byte
NOWAYOS: entropy: start-up tests passed over the first 1024 bytes, which were discarded
NOWAYOS: entropy: seed ring 0 full: 4 seeds
NOWAYOS: seed-consumer: starting
NOWAYOS: seed-consumer: not ready: a draw before its first seed is refused
NOWAYOS: seed-consumer: seeded: its generator keyed, and its copies of the seed wiped
NOWAYOS: seed-consumer: drew 32 bytes; their SHA-256 follows, never the bytes
NOWAYOS: entropy: seed ring 0: 1 taken seed(s) overwritten
NOWAYOS: seed-consumer: the slot it took no longer holds its seed

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere (substring match),
# including in the second after the last line above: a fault reported by the
# Microkit monitor, a kernel error message, a panic, a PD giving up, a failed
# health test, a refused seed or a consumer waiting for one.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!health test failed
!a seed refused
!no seed on its ring
!too few bytes
